.TH LAMP 1 "2026-08-05" "lamp 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lamp \- control the Mi Bedside Lamp 2 over the local network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lamp
[\fIargument\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls a Mi Bedside Lamp 2 (MJCTD02YL) directly over the miIO protocol on
udp/54321. Everything happens on the local network: there is no cloud round
trip, no hub, and no dependency on the Xiaomi or Yeelight apps. The lamp's
HomeKit pairing is untouched, so the Home app keeps working alongside it.
.PP
Setting a brightness or colour on a lamp that is off will also turn it on.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B (none)
Toggle power.
.TP
.BR on ", " off
Set power directly.
.TP
.B <0-100>
Set brightness as a percentage. A value of 0 turns the lamp off.
.TP
.BI <n> k
Set colour temperature in kelvin, for example
.BR "lamp 2700k" .
Values are clamped to the 1700\-6500K the device accepts. The
.B k
suffix is required, so that brightness and temperature cannot be confused.
.TP
.BR warm ", " cool
Shorthand for 2700k and 5000k.
.TP
.I name
A named colour:
.BR red ", " orange ", " amber ", " yellow ", " lime ", " green ", " mint ,
.BR teal ", " cyan ", " azure ", " blue ", " indigo ", " violet ", " purple ,
.BR magenta ", " pink ", " white .
Case-insensitive. The values are tuned for an LED rather than a screen and can
be overridden under
.B [colours]
in the configuration file.
.TP
.BI # rrggbb
Set colour by hex. The leading hash is optional. A six-letter hex word is
always read as hex, so a configured colour cannot shadow it.
.TP
.BI @ scene
Apply a named scene from the configuration file.
.TP
.B status
Print power, brightness, and current colour or temperature.
.TP
.B setup
Sign in to the Xiaomi cloud, write the device address to the configuration
file, and put the device token on the clipboard to be added to the environment.
Interactive: it asks for the account and password, and handles the captcha and
emailed two-factor code that the account may require. The password is not
echoed, and neither it nor the token is ever written to a file. Needed once, and
again only if the lamp is reset.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LAMP_TOKEN
The 32 character hex device token. Required. It is kept out of the
configuration file so that the file stays safe to read, sync and commit; put it
somewhere your shell exports but your dotfiles repository does not track, such
as
.IR ~/.zsh_secrets .
.PP
It must be exported. A bare
.B LAMP_TOKEN=...
assignment is a shell variable only, and child processes never see it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lamp/config.toml
Device address, scenes, and colour overrides. No credentials.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.EX
ip = "192.168.1.4"

[scenes.read]
brightness = 80
kelvin = 4000

[scenes.sleep]
brightness = 5
rgb = "#ff3000"

[colours]
blue = "#0033cc"
.EE
.PP
Colour overrides are applied one at a time over the built-in names, so setting
one does not remove the others.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits non-zero if the configuration is missing or invalid, if the argument is
not understood, or if the lamp does not answer. A lamp that is switched off at
the wall is reported as unreachable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swatch (1)
